{%- set banned_openings_block = "" %}
{%- if banned_openings %}
{%- set ob_lines = ["", "BANNED HOOK OPENINGS — never start any hook with these:"] %}
{%- for opening in banned_openings %}
{%- set _ = ob_lines.append('  ✗ "' ~ opening ~ '"') %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- set _ = ob_lines.append("") %}
{%- set _ = ob_lines.append("") %}
{%- set banned_openings_block = ob_lines | join("\n") %}
{%- endif %}
{%- set banned_hashtag_block = "" %}
{%- if banned_words %}
{%- set vocab = [] %}
{%- for w in banned_words %}
{%- set _ = vocab.append("#" ~ (w | replace(" ", ""))) %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- set hb_lines = ["", "BANNED HASHTAG VOCABULARY: " ~ (vocab | join(", ")), "Never use these or close variations as hashtags.", ""] %}
{%- set banned_hashtag_block = hb_lines | join("\n") %}
{%- endif %}

{{ brand_context }}

{{ language_line }}

Generate exactly {{ hook_count }} alternative opening hook{{ "" if hook_count == 1 else "s" }} for the content below.
{% if hook_count > 1 %}Each hook must use a distinctly different structural approach.{% endif %}

Hook 1 — Contrarian: Challenge a common belief or assumption the audience holds.
{% if hook_count >= 2 %}Hook 2 — Specific outcome: Lead with a concrete number, result, timeframe, or outcome that appears in the content. If the content has none, lead with a named detail instead and use no number.
{% endif %}{% if hook_count >= 3 %}Hook 3 — Plain observation: State something specific the audience already feels but rarely says, in a calm, direct voice. Do not use the words "uncomfortable truth".
{% endif %}{% if hook_count >= 4 %}Hook 4 — Question: Ask one specific question the audience is already asking themselves, based on the content.
{% endif %}{% if hook_count >= 5 %}Hook 5 — Scene: Open on one small, concrete moment from the content that puts the reader inside the situation.
{% endif %}
Rules for all hooks:
- Maximum 2 sentences each
- Must match the brand voice exactly
- Must be suitable for {{ platform_label }}
- Score each 1-10 for scroll-stopping power (be honest — most hooks are 5-7)
- Use only specific details from the brand story — never invented statistics
{{ banned_openings_block }}{{ banned_hashtag_block }}
CONTENT:
{{ content | untrusted("source_content") }}

Return valid JSON only:
{
  "hooks": [
{%- for i in range(hook_count) %}
    {"text": "...", "style": "{{ ['Contrarian', 'Specific outcome', 'Plain observation', 'Question', 'Scene'][i] }}", "score": 7}{{ "," if not loop.last else "" }}
{%- endfor %}
  ],
  "recommended": 0
}

The recommended field is the index (0 to {{ hook_count - 1 }}) of the highest scoring hook.
